From 75680ae7b315ac5fc9572e8f2bba87e591555f50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 12:09:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Weight the numeric tier's refusals by the boxes they cost

0105 put 44.36% of the corpus's guarded-tree root boxes into a local and
left two candidate explanations. The cheap one is a seam: the tier had
already accepted the destination, and the box is minted by the tree and
unboxed by the very next instruction, because the assignment path asks
for the right-hand side as a JSValue whenever the STATIC prover cannot
type it even though the whole-function prover already did. Measured, the
seam is 36 boxes of 18.6 M. It is not the explanation, and knowing that
is what makes the rest worth instrumenting.

So every one of those locals is one the tier REFUSED, and which refusal
carries the weight is a question item 3-6 answered in the wrong
currency: it counted causes per NAME, which weights a name refused in
initialization code the same as one refused inside a ten-million
iteration loop. The analysis now retains its per-name refusal and the
boxing site names it, so the causes are ranked by execution.

Of 19 005 731 such boxes over all fifteen suites:

  DroppedCandidate   7 300 519   38.41%
  ElementRead        6 908 814   36.35%
  Unknown            2 429 752   12.78%
  PropertyRead         925 292    4.87%
  Parameter            775 865    4.08%
  CallResult           274 411    1.44%
  everything else      395 078    2.07%

Two things follow. DroppedCandidate is a cascade -- a name refused only
because another refused name reaches it -- and the analysis's own note
is that fixing its root fixes it for free, so 38.41% of these boxes have
no independent cause to fix and NavierStokes at 96.8% is the roadmap's
already-recorded rowSize cascade showing up from a second direction.
And the largest independent cause is ElementRead at 36.35%, which is the
same conclusion item 3-1's guarded tree already reaches at run time: the
tree computes a[i] * b on raw doubles behind a type test and boxes the
root anyway, because the static prover and the run-time test do not
share a conclusion.

Unknown at 12.78% is a gap in the instrument, not a cause, and is
reported as such: it is a destination whose name the analysis map does
not carry.

4 further cases, the load-bearing one being that the refusals partition
the boxes counted at the site. 8 166 tests across eight projects, no
failures.
